  "version": "0.19.0",
  "notes": "Picture-drawn games (Unity, like Screw Out 3D) are played again: each tap or drag is told apart by where it lands, so one tap that did nothing no longer blocks every other move, and the screen-sized game surface is never treated as a button. Tutorials that say drag or rotate get a drag. Start Autopilot or Run Playbook on a game page now opens the Phone tab. The Phone tab's Start Autopilot button is gone: what you schedule runs at its time, one after another, with Pause queue / Resume queue. After a capture, each game shows a research bar (how to play, tips, a guide and its screenshots, Falcor's notes) and then Ready to play; Autopilot reads these notes before every move and each session's playbook builds on them.",
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-19T16:34:35.386Z",
